  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you are responsible for designing a connection strategy for an application that needs to access data stored in Firestore. To ensure optimal performance, scalability, and connection management, which of the following strategies should you use?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Connect the application instances to the nearest regional Firestore endpoint using VPC peering<br/>B. Implement a regional load balancer with regional backends to distribute connections to the nearest Firestore instance<br/>C. Utilize Firestore client libraries in the application for efficient connection management and idiomatic API for database operations<br/>D. Use a single global VPC for all application instances and Firestore instances to simplify network management",
  "domain": "Design scalable and highly available cloud database solutions",
  "hasImage": false,
